      "text": "Let's solve this step-by-step using Python to make sure the calculations are accurate.\n\n### Step 1: Apply the first discount (20% off the regular price)\n\nRegular price of the shirt:\n\\[\n30 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nFirst discount:\n\\[\n20\\% \\text{ off} = \\frac{20}{100} \\times 30 = 0.20 \\times 30 = 6 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nNew price after the first discount:\n\\[\n30 - 6 = 24 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Apply the second discount (25% off the reduced price)\n\nNew price after the first discount:\n\\[\n24 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nSecond discount:\n\\[\n25\\% \\text{ off} = \\frac{25}{100} \\times 24 = 0.25 \\times 24 = 6 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nFinal price after both discounts:\n\\[\n24 - 6 = 18 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the single percent discount needed to get to the same final price\n\nWe want:\n\\[\n18 \\text{ dollars} = x\\% \\text{ off } 30 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{30 - 18}{30} \\times 100\\% = x\\%\n\\]\n\nLet's solve this using Python to find the value of \\( x \\).\n```python\n# Regular price of the shirt\nregular_price = 30\n\n# Price after the first discount (20% off)\nprice_after_first_discount = regular_price * (1 - 0.20)\n\n# Price after the second discount (25% off)\nfinal_price = price_after_first_discount * (1 - 0.25)\n\n# Calculate the single percent discount needed to get the final price\nsingle_percent_discount = ((regular_price - final_price) / regular_price) * 100\nprint(single_percent_discount)\n```\n```output\n25.0\n```\nThe single percent discount needed to give the same final price as the two successive discounts is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
